    "rationale": "The Builder's proposal (entity0) sets the outer sensors to x = ±0.03 m with kd 0.35. The outcome table records the verified 160.5 design (iterations 7 and 8) at x = ±0.036 m, not ±0.03. Iteration 6 (±0.036, kd 0.25) scored 97.7, and iteration 7 (±0.036, kd 0.35) scored 160.5. So the large gain came from the damping change, and reach has only been tested at kd 0.15, where ±0.03 (52.2) and ±0.036 (52.4) were neutral. Racing ±0.03 with kd 0.35 is therefore a clean single-variable test of reach against the verified 160.5 design. I keep the Builder's geometry as supplied and hold the controller at the iteration 7 values (kp 2.5, ki 0.05, kd 0.35, base_speed 1.5, symmetric weights [-2,-1,0,1,2], last_direction), so the only difference from the verified design is the outer reach. Expected: oval completions near 2 of 20 with a score close to 160 if reach is neutral. If the score falls well below 160 with oval completions lost, reach was helping and the final design should revert to ±0.036. I do not change kd or wheel_track in this race, to avoid confounding the reach result.",
