    "feedback": "Written before this candidate has raced, so no outcome is stated for it. Correction to the record: the outcome table shows the verified 160.5 design (iterations 7 and 8) at outer sensors x = ±0.036 m, not ±0.03 m. The 97.7 to 160.5 gain came from raising kd from 0.25 to 0.35 on the same reach, so the reach change you attributed it to was not what drove the gain. At kd 0.15, reach was neutral: iteration 4 (±0.03) scored 52.2 and iteration 5 (±0.036) scored 52.4. I have integrated your ±0.03 layout with the iteration 7 controller, so this race is a clean test of reach alone against 160.5. Next race: if the score stays near 160 with oval completions held, reach is neutral and you can choose either layout on other grounds. If the score falls well below 160 with oval completions lost, reach was helping at kd 0.35, and the next design should return to ±0.036. If slalom line_loss_events stays at 1 or more with slalom progress below 0.16, the next lever is wheel_track 0.14, changed alone.",
